messages:
tanya: New user report: quickstart fails on Deno Deploy with `TypeError: globalThis.crypto is undefined` when calling sdk.createClient(). Works fine in Node.

omar: Deno Deploy sometimes strips webcrypto depending on the target. Are you using a CDN bundle or the npm package via skypack/esbuild?

chris: We had a repro: importing `@redwood-inference/js-sdk` from esm.sh then calling default client triggered codepath that expects Node "crypto" shim. Deno needs webcrypto (globalThis.crypto) and fetch available.

omar: Quick workaround for users: add a small prelude to set globals before importing sdk: 
```js
if (!globalThis.crypto) {
  const { webcrypto } = await import('https://deno.land/std@0.203.0/crypto/mod.ts');
  globalThis.crypto = webcrypto;
}
if (!globalThis.fetch) {
  globalThis.fetch = (await import('https://deno.land/x/fetch_polyfill@1.0.0/mod.ts')).fetch;
}
import { createClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@redwood-inference/js-sdk';
```
This unblocks most quickstarts.

tanya: That worked for me locally, but Deno Deploy still errored (Deploy runtime removes some dynamic imports). Any long-term plan?

chris: Proposal: publish a dedicated dist/deno ESM entry that only relies on Web APIs (no node:crypto or process.env reads). We can add a small deno-specific README explaining required globals and example import_map.

edge-bot: CI: flaky test alert for bun-runner in last 5 runs (retry/backoff suite). Suggested: add platform-specific test matrix.

omar: Also typing issues: Deno users often get missing DOM lib errors for Crypto types. We should ship a `deno.d.ts` that re-exports minimal dom types and a `globals.d.ts` with `declare var crypto: Crypto;` so consumers don't edit tsconfig.

chris: SDK changes needed: avoid mutating Headers (Bun freezes them), detect frozen headers with `Object.isFrozen(headers)` and copy when needed; expose `platform` option in `createClient` so users can opt into Deno/Bun-friendly behavior.

tanya: I'll add a short repro and open an issue with stack and deploy link. Thanks for the shims and plan notes.
